[native] Do nothing in ReduceMemoryUsage on a lost device

Destroy() frees the dynamic uploader, the memory block allocator and the
internal pipeline store, which ReduceMemoryUsage() then dereferences. The
caller cannot check for it: the device may be destroyed by another thread
right after. Both run under the device guard, so the check belongs here.

Drop this patch when Dawn checks the state of the device itself.

---
diff --git a/src/dawn/native/Device.cpp b/src/dawn/native/Device.cpp
--- a/src/dawn/native/Device.cpp
+++ b/src/dawn/native/Device.cpp
@@ -2702,5 +2702,8 @@
 
 bool DeviceBase::ReduceMemoryUsage() {
     DAWN_ASSERT(IsLockedByCurrentThreadIfNeeded());
+    if (IsLost()) {
+        return false;
+    }
     if (ConsumedError(GetQueue()->CheckPassedSerials())) {
         return false;
